 WORKS-13. A click can name a row.

 The arms are paired against the two ways a hit arrives and the ways it can
 miss. `ev-hit-widget` answers with the deepest node under the point, so an
 ordinary click lands on a CELL and only a click in the row's own padding
 lands on the row panel: a helper that read one shape and not the other
 would pass a test written against the shape its author had in mind and miss
 most real clicks.

 The misses matter as much: another table's id, this table's header, its
 footer, and a key that no row carries must all answer -1 rather than 0,
 because 0 is a row.

Section: Fixtures

  cols : List TableColumn = [table-column "k" "ID" 68, table-column "s" "Status" 100]

  rows : List TableRow = [
    table-row "a" ["CDX-1", "Todo"],
    table-row "b" ["CDX-2", "Done"],
    table-row "with-dash" ["CDX-3", "Todo"]
  ]

  dt : DataTableState = data-table-new "issues" cols rows

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
    print-line-uni ("row panel, first:  " & show (data-table-row-of-hit dt "issues-row-0"))
    print-line-uni ("row panel, third:  " & show (data-table-row-of-hit dt "issues-row-2"))
    print-line-uni ("cell in first row: " & show (data-table-row-of-hit dt "issues-cell-a-0"))
    print-line-uni ("cell in second:    " & show (data-table-row-of-hit dt "issues-cell-b-1"))
    print-line-uni ("a key with a dash: " & show (data-table-row-of-hit dt "issues-cell-with-dash-1"))
    print-line-uni ("a key no row has:  " & show (data-table-row-of-hit dt "issues-cell-zz-0"))
    print-line-uni ("the header:        " & show (data-table-row-of-hit dt "issues-hdr"))
    print-line-uni ("a header button:   " & show (data-table-row-of-hit dt "issues-col-1"))
    print-line-uni ("the footer:        " & show (data-table-row-of-hit dt "issues-footer"))
    print-line-uni ("another table:     " & show (data-table-row-of-hit dt "other-row-1"))
    print-line-uni ("nothing at all:    " & show (data-table-row-of-hit dt ""))

    let laid = widget-layout (data-table-widget dt) theme-terminal (layout-rect 0 0 400 200)
    in act
      print-line-uni ("through a real layout, a point in row 2: " & show (row-under laid 40 (y-of laid "issues-row-2" 6)))
      print-line-uni ("through a real layout, a point in row 0: " & show (row-under laid 40 (y-of laid "issues-row-0" 6)))
      print-line-uni ("through a real layout, the header:       " & show (row-under laid 40 (y-of laid "issues-hdr" 6)))
    end
  end

Section: Through The Layout

 The arms above feed the helper an id by hand, which tests string surgery
 and nothing else. These three go the whole way a click goes: lay the table
 out, ask `ev-hit-widget` what is under a POINT, and hand what it answers to
 the helper. That is every step of the real path except the mouse itself,
 which no bed here can press -- `desk.ps1` scripts scancodes and codex-vm
 takes `-keys` and no pointer.

  y-of : WidgetNode, Text, Integer -> Integer
  y-of (root) (id) (into) =
    when widget-find root id
      is Just (w) -> (w.wn-bounds).lr-y + into
      is None -> 0 - 1

  row-under : WidgetNode, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  row-under (laid) (x) (y) =
    when ev-hit-widget laid x y
      is Just (w) -> data-table-row-of-hit dt (w.wn-id)
      is None -> 0 - 1
